# Full-source context completion under immutable-state profile v5

The v12 run completes both full native producer/consumer roundtrips within the
unchanged 600-second per-process bound. `full_state_identity_v12_audit.json`
independently verifies the terminal process receipts, every declared Python path,
raw-file counts/bytes, prior state/root equality and the unchanged runtime source
inventory of 7,255 files. Its retained runner is `audit_full_state_identity_v12.py`.

| Repository | Regular files / Python files | Symbols / edges | Preparation wall / CPU, seconds | Producer process / consumer process, seconds |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| XML | 16 / 6 | 162 / 1,487 | 9.103 / 8.634 | 10.753 / 0.874 |
| Pyparsing | 286 / 154 | 3,957 / 55,859 | 566.254 / 553.516 | 569.609 / 1.740 |

Pyparsing also retains one opaque symlink without following it. Together the
independent consumers materialize all 302 regular files, totaling 11,781,935 bytes,
from the native Kit store. They pass eleven source/objective/policy/interface/
toolchain/environment/tampering controls each. Four descriptive Pyparsing capsules
are retained (two native exact and two conservative admissions), but no source
file is omitted. The unresolved frontier remains explicit: 1,281 XML and 46,384
Pyparsing unknown edge occurrences. No context sufficiency flag authorizes execution.

The source profile combines the earlier isolated optimizations with process-local
memoization of the canonical identity of one exact immutable native repository
state. `state_identity_cache_design_v5.md` states its boundary and assumptions.
All 159 existing relevant native regressions pass. Fresh-process parent/profile
comparisons preserve the exact serialized state, semantic root and all 1,992 XML
blocks for baseline, changed-source cold and changed-source incremental states.
The source change produces a new identity; cold and incremental results agree.
Each profile also completes twenty actual source materializations, performs forty
source fetches, and rejects twenty corrupt-source attempts. Tampered restoration,
frozen-state and dynamic-subclass controls pass.

The full Pyparsing state and root equal the preceding full-profile producer and
the independently verified 67,872-block literal-predicate audit. Full Pyparsing
cold/incremental block equality has not been measured in this v12 run; the
cross-profile cold/incremental controls above are explicitly the full XML case.

The earlier five full Pyparsing process deadlines remain retained failures of
those profiles. This is a distinct implementation profile and one shared-host run
per repository, so completion within the deadline is established without a
replicated end-to-end speedup claim. Preparation/import and consumer costs remain
chargeable. There are zero provider calls, zero signed execution receipts, zero
authorized execution/proof reuses, and no repair-quality or token-savings result.

The generic repository-context API accepts this explicit runtime inventory via
`results_v12_full_state_identity/runtime_source_manifest.json`. Existing Requests
enrollments retain their original literal-union profile and hashes. A controller
may only adopt a successor profile through a new frozen request/preparation; these
results do not silently change any earlier evaluation's implementation.
